9\. 您的项目试图解决什么问题？为何解决这个问题很重要？

What problem are you trying to solve, and why is it important?

\- Yield bearing stablecoins lack strong fundamentals, with potential loss of value under market scrutiny. Onchain RWAs can be the collateral needed for stable coins. However, they are in the hands of a few players and KYB barriers are high on time and money, creating a friction to RWA exposure in a massive way.

10\. 您提出的解决方案是什么？（请根据上一个问题来回答。）

What is your proposed solution?

\- R2USD solves by collateraling its pegged to Institutional grade tokenized RWAs. R2 diversified financial risk via asset diversification and curation in their own basket strategies. Yield is sourced from these strategies (5-10% pure RWA yield) and obtained by staking R2USD. Reaching both institutional and retail investors, sR2USD is a composable LST that allows bridging real sourced yield into DeFi native environments such as Lending or DEX protocols for yield boost. Yield is later on obtained through yield distribution and redemption mechanism set by R2. 

This product design and structure solves DeFi composability from RWA assets, Yield distributions, and Value pegging through legitimate and curated assets onchain.

11\. 竞争对手/类似产品（您的项目在Aptos生态系统内外是否有直接竞争产品或同类项目？）

Any competitions? (Does your project have direct competition or similar project on the market within or without apples ecosystem?)

For a yield bearing stablecoin, the targeted problems are mapping risks, selecting the right collateral type, sourcing the yield, and distributing the yield to users, while maintaining the peg value against the risks associated with the product composition of the stablecoin itself. The strategy on each will be tailored to retail or institutions, but it falls into one or the other. We saw a lack of a fundamental standard for yield bearing stablecoins

* Direct competitors are other yield bearing stablecoins: DeFi Native (OUSD, CAP), RWA Backed (USDY, USDM), Synthetic/Algorithmic (USDe, USDf). While indirect competitors monetize on demand and transaction fees: Fiat Backed (USDC, USDT). We don't count crypto collateralized stables as competitors due to the high volatility on the underlying assets plus no APY.  
* Through R2USD we cover 3 main risk kinds common among the yield bearing classes: issuer risk (interest rate fluctuations, USDM and USDY), smart contract risk (platform dependency, OUSD), and Depeg Risk (Loss of Confidence, USDe and USDf). We distribute issuer risk through diversifying onchain tokenized RWA strategies (T-Bills, MMFs, Private Credit/Loans), smart contract risk through having a fundamental yield purely on RWA assets (5-10% APY) and tapping into different DeFi strategies on top of fundamentals (Morpho, Pendle, Curve, Aave, etc), and depegging risk by adjusting RWA vaults based on sharp ratios, APY, and user demand (financial and legal engineering)  
* With on-chain RWA fundamentals, we detach from centralization and Custody risk (USDT, USDC) in regards to the underlying assets backing R2USD, while RWA assets also help to avoid liquidation and high volatility from crypto (DAI). 


12\. 为什么选择Aptos？

Why Aptos？

\- Move language: Move is built for asset safety which ideal for stablecoins and tokenized assets. Besides, this can support further composability towards further integration with Moved language protocols and ecosystems in the later future, being Aptos a catalyst to it.

\- Novel Case: fewer stablecoins \= more visibility and adoption opportunities for R2USD. For TVL and incentive on boosted yield, it can create a great channel for r2 to source liquidity and a great value proposition for the Aptos ecosystem and community to tap into tokenized asset in DeFi

\- Strategic Ecosystem Fit: It is easier to become a “default stablecoin” in certain protocols. Aptos needs stable rails like R2USD for:

* Lending/borrowing  
* DEX trading pairs  
* On/off-ramping of RWAs

\-Scalability and Efficiency: R2USD won’t face gas spikes or congestion in peak times due to the Aptos chain latency and infra. This will support ideally use cases like: 

* Payments & Micro-transactions  
* Yield protocols

